# Kaggle v13 Output lands here. Nothing in this folder is tracked except the two files that
# explain it.
#
# The checkpoints are 332 MB each, 1.6 GB total, and must never reach git. The root
# .gitignore covers *.pth, *.pth.tar and *.ckpt, but not the two shapes they arrive in:
# Kaggle serves an Output download as a .zip, and a torch checkpoint IS a zip container, so
# double-clicking one gets it unpacked by macOS Archive Utility into a directory of raw
# tensor shards (data/0, data/1, ...) and one checkpoint becomes ~240 files.
#
# The small artifacts are not tracked either. This folder is staging for a Kaggle upload,
# not a record. They are byte-identical to the copies already archived under
# results/06-ddpm-line-emission/v13_2026-08-12T0450_19efd47/, which is the record
# (RULES.md #5), and a second tracked copy is how a folder starts disagreeing with its
# archive.
*
!README.md
!.gitignore
